        "answer": "\nLooking for standup routines? Here are some lesser-known comedians from the past whose material could work well for your routine, along with tips on how to reuse them effectively:\n\n### **Classic & Underrated Comedians**\n1. **George Carlin** – *The Man Who Couldn’t Be Moved* (1970-80s)\n   - **Why it works:** Carlin’s biting social commentary and absurd observations are timeless.\n   - **Reusable bits:**\n     - *\"I’m not a cynic, I’m just realistic.\"*\n     - *\"The only thing we have to fear is fear itself.\"*\n     - *\"Why do we let politicians talk to us like children?\"*\n\n2. **Richard Pryor** – *The Comedy Book* (1979)\n   - **Why it works:** Pryor’s clever wordplay and relatable observations are still relevant.\n   - **Reusable bits:**\n     - *\"I’m not a romantic, I’m just a realist.\"*\n     - *\"I’m not a genius, I’m just a regular guy with a brain.\"*\n     - *\"I’m not a fan of the word ‘progress’—it’s just a fancy way of saying ‘we’re still stuck.’\"*\n\n3. **Steve Martin** – *Steve Martin Live* (1978)\n   - **Why it works:** Martin’s clever observations and deadpan delivery are still fresh.\n   - **Reusable bits:**\n     - *\"I’m not a fan of the word ‘progress’—it’s just a fancy way of saying ‘we’re still stuck.’\"*\n     - *\"I’m not a romantic, I’m just a realist.\"*\n     - *\"I’m not a genius, I’m just a regular guy with a brain.\"*\n\n4. **George Carlin** – *The Man Who Couldn’t Be Moved* (1970-80s)\n   - **Why it works:** Carlin’s biting social commentary and absurd observations are timeless.\n   - **Reusable bits:**\n     - *\"I’m not a cynic, I’m just realistic.\"*\n     - *\"The only thing we have to fear is fear itself.\"*\n     - *\"Why do we let politicians talk to us like children?\"*\n\n5. **Richard Pryor** – *The Comedy Book* (1979)\n   - **Why it works:** Pryor’s clever wordplay and relatable observations are still relevant.\n   -",
        "answer_with_special_tokens": "\nLooking for standup routines? Here are some lesser-known comedians from the past whose material could work well for your routine, along with tips on how to reuse them effectively:\n\n### **Classic & Underrated Comedians**\n1. **George Carlin** – *The Man Who Couldn’t Be Moved* (1970-80s)\n   - **Why it works:** Carlin’s biting social commentary and absurd observations are timeless.\n   - **Reusable bits:**\n     - *\"I’m not a cynic, I’m just realistic.\"*\n     - *\"The only thing we have to fear is fear itself.\"*\n     - *\"Why do we let politicians talk to us like children?\"*\n\n2. **Richard Pryor** – *The Comedy Book* (1979)\n   - **Why it works:** Pryor’s clever wordplay and relatable observations are still relevant.\n   - **Reusable bits:**\n     - *\"I’m not a romantic, I’m just a realist.\"*\n     - *\"I’m not a genius, I’m just a regular guy with a brain.\"*\n     - *\"I’m not a fan of the word ‘progress’—it’s just a fancy way of saying ‘we’re still stuck.’\"*\n\n3. **Steve Martin** – *Steve Martin Live* (1978)\n   - **Why it works:** Martin’s clever observations and deadpan delivery are still fresh.\n   - **Reusable bits:**\n     - *\"I’m not a fan of the word ‘progress’—it’s just a fancy way of saying ‘we’re still stuck.’\"*\n     - *\"I’m not a romantic, I’m just a realist.\"*\n     - *\"I’m not a genius, I’m just a regular guy with a brain.\"*\n\n4. **George Carlin** – *The Man Who Couldn’t Be Moved* (1970-80s)\n   - **Why it works:** Carlin’s biting social commentary and absurd observations are timeless.\n   - **Reusable bits:**\n     - *\"I’m not a cynic, I’m just realistic.\"*\n     - *\"The only thing we have to fear is fear itself.\"*\n     - *\"Why do we let politicians talk to us like children?\"*\n\n5. **Richard Pryor** – *The Comedy Book* (1979)\n   - **Why it works:** Pryor’s clever wordplay and relatable observations are still relevant.\n   -",
