        "answer": "\nI understand your frustration, and I’m here to help you set up a **legally sound credit card charge dispute** to recover your money. Here’s a step-by-step guide tailored to your situation:\n\n### **1. Gather Evidence**\nCollect all items you received, including:\n- **Receipts** (with dates, store name, and product details).\n- **Proof of purchase** (e.g., email confirmation, receipt scan, or loyalty card).\n- **Photos/videos** of the products in their original packaging.\n- **Proof of purchase price** (e.g., receipt, loyalty card, or online order history).\n\n### **2. Understand Your Options**\n- **Return Window Missed**: If the store’s return policy allows returns within a short period (e.g., 7 days), you may still have recourse.\n- **Credit Card Dispute**: A chargeback is the most effective way to recover your money, but it’s not a guarantee.\n\n### **3. Contact the Store**\n- **Phone**: Call the store’s customer service and explain your situation. Ask if they can process a return or refund.\n- **Email**: Send a polite email to the store, including:\n  - Your order details (date, item, price).\n  - Proof of purchase.\n  - A request for a refund or return.\n  - Your credit card details (if applicable).\n\n### **4. File a Chargeback**\nIf the store refuses to process a return, file a chargeback with your credit card issuer. Provide:\n- **Proof of purchase** (receipts, emails, etc.).\n- **Proof of return attempt** (store’s response, if any).\n- **Details of the products** (name, brand, model, etc.).\n- **Reason for dispute** (e.g., \"Return window missed\").\n\n### **5. Credit Card Dispute Process**\n- **Contact the Card Issuer**: Call or visit your bank to initiate a chargeback.\n- **Provide Documentation**: Share all evidence with your bank.\n- **Wait for Resolution**: The bank will review the dispute and either approve the chargeback or decline it.\n\n### **6. Additional Tips**\n- **Be Polite and Professional**: Maintain a respectful tone in all communications.\n- **Follow Up**: If you don’t receive a response, follow up with the store and bank.\n- **Know Your Rights**: Familiarize yourself with your credit card issuer’s chargeback policy.\n\n### **7. Legal Considerations**\n- **Return Policy",
        "answer_with_special_tokens": "\nI understand your frustration, and I’m here to help you set up a **legally sound credit card charge dispute** to recover your money. Here’s a step-by-step guide tailored to your situation:\n\n### **1. Gather Evidence**\nCollect all items you received, including:\n- **Receipts** (with dates, store name, and product details).\n- **Proof of purchase** (e.g., email confirmation, receipt scan, or loyalty card).\n- **Photos/videos** of the products in their original packaging.\n- **Proof of purchase price** (e.g., receipt, loyalty card, or online order history).\n\n### **2. Understand Your Options**\n- **Return Window Missed**: If the store’s return policy allows returns within a short period (e.g., 7 days), you may still have recourse.\n- **Credit Card Dispute**: A chargeback is the most effective way to recover your money, but it’s not a guarantee.\n\n### **3. Contact the Store**\n- **Phone**: Call the store’s customer service and explain your situation. Ask if they can process a return or refund.\n- **Email**: Send a polite email to the store, including:\n  - Your order details (date, item, price).\n  - Proof of purchase.\n  - A request for a refund or return.\n  - Your credit card details (if applicable).\n\n### **4. File a Chargeback**\nIf the store refuses to process a return, file a chargeback with your credit card issuer. Provide:\n- **Proof of purchase** (receipts, emails, etc.).\n- **Proof of return attempt** (store’s response, if any).\n- **Details of the products** (name, brand, model, etc.).\n- **Reason for dispute** (e.g., \"Return window missed\").\n\n### **5. Credit Card Dispute Process**\n- **Contact the Card Issuer**: Call or visit your bank to initiate a chargeback.\n- **Provide Documentation**: Share all evidence with your bank.\n- **Wait for Resolution**: The bank will review the dispute and either approve the chargeback or decline it.\n\n### **6. Additional Tips**\n- **Be Polite and Professional**: Maintain a respectful tone in all communications.\n- **Follow Up**: If you don’t receive a response, follow up with the store and bank.\n- **Know Your Rights**: Familiarize yourself with your credit card issuer’s chargeback policy.\n\n### **7. Legal Considerations**\n- **Return Policy",
