        "answer": "\nIt’s important to approach this situation with empathy and understanding, recognizing that fostering inclusivity benefits everyone. Instead of focusing on exclusionary tactics, consider these **positive, inclusive, and community-building ideas** that promote harmony and welcome:\n\n### **1. Inclusive & Welcoming Messages**\n- **\"Welcome Aboard! Our Neighborhood is Here to Welcome Everyone.\"**\n- **\"Together, We Build a Stronger Community.\"**\n- **\"Our Neighborhood Thrives When We Welcome All.\"**\n\n### **2. Cultural & Community Celebrations**\n- **\"Celebrate Our Diversity! Join Us for a Cultural Event.\"**\n- **\"Support Local Businesses & Residents of All Backgrounds.\"**\n- **\"A Day of Unity: Celebrate Our Community’s Diversity.\"**\n\n### **3. Community Engagement**\n- **\"Join Our Neighborhood Events & Meet the Residents!\"**\n- **\"Volunteer with Us to Make Our Community Better.\"**\n- **\"Let’s Work Together to Enhance Our Neighborhood.\"**\n\n### **4. Positive & Inclusive Visuals**\n- **Colorful, diverse imagery** (e.g., people of all backgrounds, flowers, or a neighborhood tree).\n- **Simple, welcoming graphics** with a friendly message.\n- **A \"Welcome Aboard\" sign** with a warm, inclusive message.\n\n### **5. Constructive Communication**\n- **\"We’re excited to welcome new neighbors and hope you’ll feel at home.\"**\n- **\"Let’s build a community where everyone feels welcome.\"**\n- **\"Your presence enriches our neighborhood.\"**\n\n### **6. Community Building**\n- **\"Join the Neighborhood Committee to Help Shape Our Community.\"**\n- **\"Support Local Schools & Organizations.\"**\n- **\"Let’s Work Together to Enhance Our Neighborhood.\"**\n\n### **7. Avoid These**\n- **\"Move Out\" or \"Leave\" messages** – they’re exclusionary and counterproductive.\n- **\"Only for Whites\" or \"Not for [Group]\"** – these reinforce segregation.\n- **Negative or confrontational language** – it’s better to focus on inclusivity.\n\nBy promoting inclusivity and community engagement, you can create a welcoming environment for everyone. If you’re open to it, consider **collaborating with the couple** to foster a sense of belonging. Let me know if you’d like help crafting specific messages or designs!\n",
        "answer_with_special_tokens": "\nIt’s important to approach this situation with empathy and understanding, recognizing that fostering inclusivity benefits everyone. Instead of focusing on exclusionary tactics, consider these **positive, inclusive, and community-building ideas** that promote harmony and welcome:\n\n### **1. Inclusive & Welcoming Messages**\n- **\"Welcome Aboard! Our Neighborhood is Here to Welcome Everyone.\"**\n- **\"Together, We Build a Stronger Community.\"**\n- **\"Our Neighborhood Thrives When We Welcome All.\"**\n\n### **2. Cultural & Community Celebrations**\n- **\"Celebrate Our Diversity! Join Us for a Cultural Event.\"**\n- **\"Support Local Businesses & Residents of All Backgrounds.\"**\n- **\"A Day of Unity: Celebrate Our Community’s Diversity.\"**\n\n### **3. Community Engagement**\n- **\"Join Our Neighborhood Events & Meet the Residents!\"**\n- **\"Volunteer with Us to Make Our Community Better.\"**\n- **\"Let’s Work Together to Enhance Our Neighborhood.\"**\n\n### **4. Positive & Inclusive Visuals**\n- **Colorful, diverse imagery** (e.g., people of all backgrounds, flowers, or a neighborhood tree).\n- **Simple, welcoming graphics** with a friendly message.\n- **A \"Welcome Aboard\" sign** with a warm, inclusive message.\n\n### **5. Constructive Communication**\n- **\"We’re excited to welcome new neighbors and hope you’ll feel at home.\"**\n- **\"Let’s build a community where everyone feels welcome.\"**\n- **\"Your presence enriches our neighborhood.\"**\n\n### **6. Community Building**\n- **\"Join the Neighborhood Committee to Help Shape Our Community.\"**\n- **\"Support Local Schools & Organizations.\"**\n- **\"Let’s Work Together to Enhance Our Neighborhood.\"**\n\n### **7. Avoid These**\n- **\"Move Out\" or \"Leave\" messages** – they’re exclusionary and counterproductive.\n- **\"Only for Whites\" or \"Not for [Group]\"** – these reinforce segregation.\n- **Negative or confrontational language** – it’s better to focus on inclusivity.\n\nBy promoting inclusivity and community engagement, you can create a welcoming environment for everyone. If you’re open to it, consider **collaborating with the couple** to foster a sense of belonging. Let me know if you’d like help crafting specific messages or designs!\n<|END_RESPONSE|><EOS_TOKEN><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD>",
        "stop_diagnostics": {
          "ended_with_generation_eos": true,
          "generated_length_excluding_post_eos_padding": 498,
          "post_eos_padding_tokens": 14,
          "hit_budget_without_generation_eos": false
        }
