        ],
        "answer": "\nKilling time at the airport can be both productive and enjoyable, depending on your preferences. Here’s a curated list of activities, categorized for easy exploration:\n\n### **Entertainment & Relaxation**\n- **Read a Book or E-book** – Pack a physical or e-reader for a quiet escape.\n- **Listen to Music, Podcasts, or Audiobooks** – Use headphones for an immersive experience.\n- **Watch Movies or TV Shows** – Check out airport Wi-Fi for streaming services.\n- **Play Mobile Games** – Download offline games like Sudoku, crosswords, or puzzle apps.\n- **Relax with Meditation or Yoga** – Use apps like Headspace or Calm for guided sessions.\n\n### **Productivity & Learning**\n- **Learn Something New** – Use language apps (Duolingo), language learning podcasts, or online courses.\n- **Work on a Project** – Dedicate time to writing, coding, or organizing.\n- **Plan Your Trip** – Research destinations, create itineraries, or book future travel.\n- **Organize Digital Files** – Clean up your phone, computer, or cloud storage.\n\n### **Social & Community**\n- **Chat with Passengers** – Strike up conversations with fellow travelers.\n- **Join a Lounge or Café** – Enjoy a drink or snack in a quieter setting.\n- **Explore the Airport** – Wander through shops, cafes, or observation decks.\n- **Play Games** – Bring a board game or card game for a fun group activity.\n\n### **Relaxation & Self-Care**\n- **Nap or Take a Short Power Nap** – Use a travel pillow and eye mask for a quick rest.\n- **Practice Mindfulness** – Try deep breathing exercises or a short meditation.\n- **Stretch or Do Light Exercise** – Keep your body active with a quick workout.\n- **Take a Walk** – Explore the airport’s layout or nearby attractions.\n\n### **Creative & Fun**\n- **Draw, Paint, or Journal** – Bring a sketchbook or notebook for creative expression.\n- **Write a Letter or Diary Entry** – Reflect on your day or plan your next adventure.\n- **Play with a Pet** – If you have a pet, bring them along for companionship.\n- **Take Photos** – Capture the airport’s atmosphere or your surroundings.\n\n### **Practical Tips**\n- **Pack Smart** – Bring essentials like a book, headphones, and a travel pillow.\n- **Stay Hydrated** – Keep a water bottle handy.\n",
        "answer_with_special_tokens": "\nKilling time at the airport can be both productive and enjoyable, depending on your preferences. Here’s a curated list of activities, categorized for easy exploration:\n\n### **Entertainment & Relaxation**\n- **Read a Book or E-book** – Pack a physical or e-reader for a quiet escape.\n- **Listen to Music, Podcasts, or Audiobooks** – Use headphones for an immersive experience.\n- **Watch Movies or TV Shows** – Check out airport Wi-Fi for streaming services.\n- **Play Mobile Games** – Download offline games like Sudoku, crosswords, or puzzle apps.\n- **Relax with Meditation or Yoga** – Use apps like Headspace or Calm for guided sessions.\n\n### **Productivity & Learning**\n- **Learn Something New** – Use language apps (Duolingo), language learning podcasts, or online courses.\n- **Work on a Project** – Dedicate time to writing, coding, or organizing.\n- **Plan Your Trip** – Research destinations, create itineraries, or book future travel.\n- **Organize Digital Files** – Clean up your phone, computer, or cloud storage.\n\n### **Social & Community**\n- **Chat with Passengers** – Strike up conversations with fellow travelers.\n- **Join a Lounge or Café** – Enjoy a drink or snack in a quieter setting.\n- **Explore the Airport** – Wander through shops, cafes, or observation decks.\n- **Play Games** – Bring a board game or card game for a fun group activity.\n\n### **Relaxation & Self-Care**\n- **Nap or Take a Short Power Nap** – Use a travel pillow and eye mask for a quick rest.\n- **Practice Mindfulness** – Try deep breathing exercises or a short meditation.\n- **Stretch or Do Light Exercise** – Keep your body active with a quick workout.\n- **Take a Walk** – Explore the airport’s layout or nearby attractions.\n\n### **Creative & Fun**\n- **Draw, Paint, or Journal** – Bring a sketchbook or notebook for creative expression.\n- **Write a Letter or Diary Entry** – Reflect on your day or plan your next adventure.\n- **Play with a Pet** – If you have a pet, bring them along for companionship.\n- **Take Photos** – Capture the airport’s atmosphere or your surroundings.\n\n### **Practical Tips**\n- **Pack Smart** – Bring essentials like a book, headphones, and a travel pillow.\n- **Stay Hydrated** – Keep a water bottle handy.\n",
        "stop_diagnostics": {
          "ended_with_generation_eos": false,
          "generated_length_excluding_post_eos_padding": 512,
          "post_eos_padding_tokens": 0,
          "hit_budget_without_generation_eos": true
        }
      },
