        ],
        "answer": "To hit your targets at work, consider the following steps:\n\n1. **Set Clear Goals**: Define specific, measurable, achievable, relevant, and time-bound (SMART) goals. This helps you focus on what needs to be accomplished.\n\n2. **Prioritize Tasks**: Identify the most important tasks that will help you reach your goals. This ensures you're using your time effectively.\n\n3. **Create a Plan**: Break down your goals into smaller, manageable tasks. This makes them less overwhelming and easier to tackle.\n\n4. **Stay Organized**: Use tools like to-do lists, calendars, or project management software to keep track of your tasks and deadlines.\n\n5. **Time Management**: Allocate specific time slots for different tasks. This can help you stay on track and avoid procrastination.\n\n6. **Take Breaks**: Regular breaks can help you stay focused and avoid burnout. Use these breaks to recharge and refocus.\n\n7. **Communicate**: Keep your team and supervisors informed about your progress. This helps in getting support and feedback when needed.\n\n8. **Review and Adjust**: Regularly review your progress and adjust your plan if necessary. This ensures you're on the right track to meet your targets.\n\n9. **Seek Support**: Don't hesitate to ask for help or resources if you need them. This can come from colleagues, supervisors, or external experts.\n\n10. **Stay Motivated**: Keep your motivation high by reminding yourself of the reasons why you set these targets. Celebrate small victories along the way.\n\nBy following these steps, you can increase your chances of hitting your targets at work.",
        "answer_with_special_tokens": "To hit your targets at work, consider the following steps:\n\n1. **Set Clear Goals**: Define specific, measurable, achievable, relevant, and time-bound (SMART) goals. This helps you focus on what needs to be accomplished.\n\n2. **Prioritize Tasks**: Identify the most important tasks that will help you reach your goals. This ensures you're using your time effectively.\n\n3. **Create a Plan**: Break down your goals into smaller, manageable tasks. This makes them less overwhelming and easier to tackle.\n\n4. **Stay Organized**: Use tools like to-do lists, calendars, or project management software to keep track of your tasks and deadlines.\n\n5. **Time Management**: Allocate specific time slots for different tasks. This can help you stay on track and avoid procrastination.\n\n6. **Take Breaks**: Regular breaks can help you stay focused and avoid burnout. Use these breaks to recharge and refocus.\n\n7. **Communicate**: Keep your team and supervisors informed about your progress. This helps in getting support and feedback when needed.\n\n8. **Review and Adjust**: Regularly review your progress and adjust your plan if necessary. This ensures you're on the right track to meet your targets.\n\n9. **Seek Support**: Don't hesitate to ask for help or resources if you need them. This can come from colleagues, supervisors, or external experts.\n\n10. **Stay Motivated**: Keep your motivation high by reminding yourself of the reasons why you set these targets. Celebrate small victories along the way.\n\nBy following these steps, you can increase your chances of hitting your targets at work.<|END_RESPONSE|><EOS_TOKEN><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD><PAD>",
        "stop_diagnostics": {
